# i18n

- Django gettext only — `USE_I18N`, `LANGUAGES`, `LOCALE_PATHS`, `LocaleMiddleware` (after `SessionMiddleware`).
- Generated languages: {% if cookiecutter.i18n_mode == "bilingual" %}English + Persian (`en`, `fa`){% else %}English only (`en`){% endif %}. Source of truth is `LANGUAGES` in `config/settings/i18n.py` — never hardcode a language list in scripts.
- User-facing strings: `_()` / `gettext_lazy`; prefer **lowercase space-separated** English msgids.
- Starter `.po` catalogs ship under `locale/<code>/LC_MESSAGES/` for generated languages.
- Refresh catalogs: `python manage.py update_translations` · `make translations` · `./scripts/update_translations.sh`. Defaults to **every** code in `settings.LANGUAGES` (0–N). Override with `--locale xx` (repeatable). Compile with `--compile` (shell also accepts legacy `--compile-messages`).
- **Add another language:** (1) append `("xx", "Name")` to `LANGUAGES` (2) `python manage.py update_translations --locale xx` (3) translate `locale/xx/LC_MESSAGES/django.po` (4) `--compile` or deploy-time `compilemessages`. No script edits required.
- Language switch: `POST /i18n/setlang/` (Django). APIs also honor `Accept-Language` via `LocaleMiddleware`.
- Default language: `.env` `LANGUAGE_CODE` (fallback `en`).
- Do not invent a second i18n stack.
- Changing languages / middleware / translation commands → update **this rule file** + `docs/style-guide/ops/translations.md` (+ `commands` / `AGENTS.md` if entrypoints change) in the **same** change.

Deep: `docs/style-guide/ops/translations.md`
